<script server>
/*
 * Blog post. The body is the club's own writing, ported across; everything
 * around it — the header, the meta line, the neighbours at the foot — is
 * derived from the shared post index so no fact is stated twice.
 */

import { articleJsonLd, neighbours, posts } from '../../site/blog'
import { cardFor, cardHeight, cardType, cardWidth } from '../../site/social'
import { club, footerColumns, hours, legalLinks, navLinks, siteUrl } from '../../site/club'

const slug = 'hyrox-training-in-santa-monica'
const post = posts.find(p => p.slug === slug)
const { prev, next } = neighbours(slug)
const path = `/blog/${slug}`
</script>

@nolayout

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    @include('site/head', {
      title: `${post.title} - TRIFIT LA`,
      description: post.excerpt,
      path,
      siteUrl,
      card: cardFor(path),
      cardType,
      cardWidth,
      cardHeight,
      cardAlt: post.title,
      ogType: 'article',
      jsonLd: articleJsonLd(post, siteUrl),
    })
  </head>

  <body>
    @include('site/nav', { navLinks, current: '/blog' })

    <main>
      <article>
        <header class="page-head">
          <div class="shell">
            <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
              <a data-stx-link href="/">Home</a>
              <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
              <a data-stx-link href="/blog">Blog</a>
              <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
              <span>{{ post.topic }}</span>
            </nav>
            <span class="eyebrow">{{ post.topic }}</span>
            <h1>{{ post.title }}</h1>
            <div class="article-meta">
              <time datetime="{{ post.date }}">{{ post.dateLabel }}</time>
              <span>{{ post.minutes }} minute read</span>
              <span>TRIFIT LA</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </header>

        <div class="section shell">
          <figure class="prose-figure post-hero">
            <StxImage :src="post.image" :alt="post.alt" width="1400" height="933" lazy="false" placeholder="blur" fetchpriority="high" />
          </figure>

          <div class="prose">
      <p>HYROX is one of the fastest-growing fitness competitions in the world — and it's rapidly gaining traction among athletes and everyday fitness enthusiasts in Santa Monica.</p>
      <p><strong>If you've searched:</strong> “HYROX training near me” “How to train for HYROX” “HYROX gym in Santa Monica”</p>
      <p>You're likely looking for a facility that can support both endurance and strength training in one place.</p>
      <h2>What Is HYROX?</h2>
      <p>HYROX is an indoor hybrid fitness race combining 8 x 1km runs with functional workout stations. Every race follows the same format, making it measurable and competitive worldwide.</p>
      <p>The race includes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>8 x 1 km runs</li>
        <li>SkiErg</li>
        <li>Sled push</li>
        <li>Sled pull</li>
        <li>Burpee broad jumps</li>
        <li>Rowing</li>
        <li>Farmer's carry</li>
        <li>Sandbag lunges</li>
        <li>Wall balls</li>
      </ul>
      <p>It's a true test of endurance, strength, power, and mental toughness — making it ideal for anyone who wants more than just a typical gym routine.</p>
      <p>Preparing for HYROX requires strategic training. It's not just about running more miles or lifting heavier weights — it's about combining both intelligently.</p>
      <h2>1. Build Your Aerobic Engine</h2>
      <p>Because you'll run 8 total kilometers during the race, endurance is critical. Training should include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Zone 2 aerobic conditioning</li>
        <li>Tempo runs</li>
        <li>Interval training</li>
        <li>Row and SkiErg conditioning sessions</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>2. Develop Functional Strength</h2>
      <p>HYROX demands real-world, repeatable strength. Key focus areas include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Heavy sled pushes and pulls</li>
        <li>Grip strength for farmer's carries</li>
        <li>Lower-body stamina for lunges and wall balls</li>
        <li>Total-body power for rowing and burpees</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>3. Train Under Fatigue</h2>
      <p>The most challenging part of HYROX is transitioning from a hard run directly into a strength movement.</p>
      <p>Example hybrid sessions:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>1 km run → sled push intervals</li>
        <li>Row → wall balls</li>
        <li>Burpee broad jumps → farmer's carries</li>
      </ul>
      <p>This style of training builds durability, efficiency, and race-day confidence.</p>
      <p>Training for HYROX requires space, equipment availability, and the ability to move seamlessly between cardio and strength stations. Not every gym can support that.</p>
      <p>At TRIFIT LA, members have access to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Open turf for sled pushes and pulls</li>
        <li>Full free-weight area for progressive strength training</li>
        <li>Rowers, SkiErgs, treadmills, and bikes</li>
        <li>Functional training space for hybrid circuits</li>
        <li>A high-energy, performance-focused environment</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You get the versatility of a large gym with the energy of a local Santa Monica fitness community.</p>
      <p>Whether you're preparing for your first HYROX or aiming to improve your race time, TRIFIT LA provides everything you need in one place.</p>
      <p>Ready to start training for HYROX in Santa Monica? Come tour TRIFIT LA and begin building your strength, endurance, and competitive edge today.</p>
          </div>

          <nav class="post-nav" aria-label="More posts">
            @if (prev)
              <a data-stx-link href="/blog/{{ prev.slug }}">
                <span>Older</span>
                <b>{{ prev.title }}</b>
              </a>
            @else
              <span></span>
            @endif
            @if (next)
              <a data-stx-link class="is-next" href="/blog/{{ next.slug }}">
                <span>Newer</span>
                <b>{{ next.title }}</b>
              </a>
            @endif
          </nav>
        </div>
      </article>

      <section class="section--tight shell">
        <div class="closer">
          <div>
            <h2>Come and see the club for yourself.</h2>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p>Call ahead for a tour, or try everything for a day with a $39 day pass.</p>
            <div class="hero-cta">
              <a data-stx-link class="btn btn--primary" href="/visit-us">Book a tour</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    @include('site/footer', { club, hours, footerColumns, legalLinks })
  </body>
</html>
